1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:04,462
One dashboard change. A focused APEX update.

2
00:00:05,223 --> 00:00:10,097
APEXREST connects Codex and Claude Code to Oracle APEX development.

3
00:00:10,107 --> 00:00:14,131
Describe what you need; the agent edits APEXlang source,

4
00:00:14,141 --> 00:00:17,770
and the plugin handles validation, planning, and import.

5
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:21,440
Here, we add a monthly-sales chart to one dashboard.

6
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:24,674
A selective export brings that page into the project.

7
00:00:24,684 --> 00:00:29,115
After editing, APEXREST identifies the changed page files.

8
00:00:29,842 --> 00:00:32,904
The change is compiled and checked against the target.

9
00:00:32,914 --> 00:00:34,863
A plan selects the right scope.

10
00:00:34,873 --> 00:00:39,017
In automatic mode, supported page changes use a file import;

11
00:00:39,027 --> 00:00:42,083
broader changes use the full application.

12
00:00:42,655 --> 00:00:46,526
Before applying, APEXREST saves an APEXlang snapshot.

13
00:00:46,536 --> 00:00:50,750
It imports the selected files and reads the page back from Oracle.

14
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:54,835
If the outcome is uncertain, recovery first checks the server.

15
00:00:55,335 --> 00:01:00,142
Shared components, such as a list of values, can also be imported separately.

16
00:01:00,152 --> 00:01:04,547
Their server observation currently uses a full APEXlang snapshot.

17
00:01:04,557 --> 00:01:09,046
Global settings and unsupported changes require a full import.

18
00:01:09,596 --> 00:01:14,144
Version two adds scoped updates and APEXlang recovery snapshots,

19
00:01:14,154 --> 00:01:16,020
with a shorter change cycle.

20
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:20,056
Compilation and planning are included in one apply workflow,

21
00:01:20,066 --> 00:01:22,295
shared by Codex and Claude Code.

22
00:01:22,845 --> 00:01:25,691
Change what matters. Keep the workflow clear.

23
00:01:25,701 --> 00:01:29,853
Explore the APEXREST 2.0 source bundle on GitHub.

